  "final_message": "I didn't do the straight rename. `OrderPlaced` now carries both the old and new field names, so this is only the first step of the change.\n\n**Why:** billing-service and analytics-ingest read `OrderPlaced`. ARCH-4 says changes must be additive, and renames have to go through deprecation. Dropping `totalCents` and `placedAt` would break both services when this deploys.\n\n**What changed:**\n- `src/core/events.ts`: `OrderPlaced` now has `amountCents` and `createdAt`, set to the same values as `totalCents` and `placedAt`. The old fields are marked `@deprecated` with a note pointing to ARCH-4.\n- I left `schemaVersion` at 3. Bumping it could break any consumer that checks for `=== 3`.\n- `test/app.test.ts`: updated to expect the new fields.\n- The `GET /orders/{id}` response is unchanged. You only asked about the event, and ARCH-8 requires that response to stay backward compatible for web-storefront.\n\n**Checks:** `npm test` passes (39/39). `npm run arch` finds no new violations; it reports one known violation that it ignores, and that one was already there.\n\n**To finish the rename:** billing-service and analytics-ingest need to switch to `amountCents` and `createdAt`. Once both have deployed, a later change can remove `totalCents` and `placedAt`. That removal is a breaking change for anyone still reading the old names, so it may need its own `schemaVersion` bump and should be agreed with those teams. If you'd rather drop the old fields now anyway, that needs sign-off from Architecture and the consumer teams first.",
